SOUNDPROBE(1)

NAME
    soundprobe - exercise SmallOS sound devices

SYNOPSIS
    soundprobe

DESCRIPTION
    Plays short diagnostic samples through the SmallOS sound syscall surface.
    The probe checks Sound Blaster digital playback paths and emits an
    AdLib/OPL2 tone when an AdLib-compatible device is present.

NOTES
    For QEMU Wolf3D testing, expose SB16 for digitized effects and AdLib for
    FM sound effects and music:

        -audiodev sdl,id=audio0,out.frequency=48000,out.buffer-length=50000
        -device sb16,audiodev=audio0,iobase=0x220,irq=5,dma=1,dma16=5
        -device adlib,audiodev=audio0

SEE ALSO
    wolf3d(1), smallos(7)
